# EduQuiz Bot — Alembic Migrations

This directory contains database schema migration files managed by Alembic.

## Quick Start

All commands must be run from the `eduquiz_bot/` directory with `DATABASE_URL` set.

### Generate a new migration (after changing models.py)
```bash
cd eduquiz_bot
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:pass@localhost/db alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add_new_column"
```

### Apply all pending migrations
```bash
cd eduquiz_bot
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:pass@localhost/db alembic upgrade head
```

### Roll back the last migration
```bash
cd eduquiz_bot
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:pass@localhost/db alembic downgrade -1
```

### Show migration history
```bash
cd eduquiz_bot
alembic history --verbose
```

## In Docker / Production

The `entrypoint.sh` automatically runs `alembic upgrade head` before starting the app.
This ensures the database schema is always up-to-date on deployment.

## Notes

- Never edit migration files after they have been applied to a shared database.
- Always review autogenerated migrations before applying them.
- For SQLite (dev only): `init_db()` handles schema creation; Alembic is for PostgreSQL.
